in other news this morning an airport  wide power outage caused chaos at one of  the nation's busiest airports last night  Airport is losing power Reagan National  Airport outside Washington lost  electricity for about 90 minutes dozens  of flights were delayed and passengers  were stranded on the tarmac Kris Van  Cleave is at the airport at Arlington  Virginia Chris the lights are back on  this morning good morning the lights are  back on this outage hit a little before  10 o'clock last night when both of the  power feeds that come into Reagan  National stopped receiving power from  utility dominion Virginia frightened  passengers posted pictures and video to  social media of the near blackout  conditions in the terminals TSA  checkpoints briefly lost power but  passengers were eventually screened  during the outage flights were held for  a time without the use of electric jet  bridges passengers were stuck on the  tarmac waiting to deplane in some cases  for over an hour they had to use air  stairs generators provided emergency  lighting to parts of the terminal in  critical operating systems like the  control tower and runway lights  firefighters were called when a  generator started to smoke but no fire  was found fortunately this happened at  basically the slowest time at Reagan  National Airport still two American  flights were canceled for Southwest  flights diverted to nearby BWI dominion  Virginia tells CBS News they're still  investigating why the lights went out  they're back on and flights are  operating normally today all right  that's good news thank you Chris
 

